i15|n|Any part of a curved line. ; Usually a curved member made up of separate wedge-shaped solids, with the joints between them disposed in the direction of the radii of the curve; used to support the wall or other weight above an opening. In this sense arches are segmental, round (i. e., semicircular), or pointed. ; A flat arch is a member constructed of stones cut into wedges or other shapes so as to support each other without rising in a curve. ; Any place covered by an arch; an archway; as, to pass into the arch of a bridge. ; Any curvature in the form of an arch; as, the arch of the aorta. ; A chief.	a:auk5,123,5;fnp,108,14;36yo,101,9;23dm,94,2;9v21,93,4;eq1,92,2;1bio,87,18;8geg,81,10;704x,80,5;3t5k,76,19;5jhi,71,7;5k7t,66,28;6vnj,64,36;7u7g,64,14;7bc3,60,7~86xk,27,347;4lq6,37,126;43ai,22,123;61gx,51,62;6kus,30,57;54q5,22,48;6vnj,64,36;3h0d,34,35;5a7n,9,33;5k7t,66,28;27ys,31,21;3t5k,76,19;3el,5,19;4j9g,11,18;1bio,87,18	v:4j9g,38,116;iyp,33,1;86xk,31,476;4j8a,30,212;7u7g,25,1;3zd0,24,1;1pct,22,3;789p,20,29;8npb,19,1;i15,14,2;8707,11,31;a7g2,8,628;ix3,4,4;8lbp,3,2;4epj,2,23~a7g2,8,628;86xk,31,476;4j8a,30,212;4j9g,38,116;8707,11,31;789p,20,29;4epj,2,23;ix3,4,4;1pct,22,3;8lbp,3,2;i15,14,2;7u7g,25,1;8npb,19,1;3zd0,24,1;iyp,33,1	V:2cbn,115,3;1asv,67,11;58rd,65,1;5h80,54,3;2dz5,44,2;actr,36,1;3fl7,21,7;7xop,17,6;2j7h,16,2;5a7n,16,52;37fa,16,2;3fkw,13,9;sbb,11,111;ajvx,11,10;a7cv,7,58~sbb,11,111;a7cv,7,58;5a7n,16,52;1asv,67,11;ajvx,11,10;3fkw,13,9;99zd,0,8;3fl7,21,7;7xop,17,6;5h80,54,3;2cbn,115,3;37fa,16,2;3lrh,6,2;2j7h,16,2;2dz5,44,2	n:6l24,110,3;415p,105,17;23dm,100,3;1eih,91,41;28pq,84,2;9v21,83,2;40qz,70,56;iyp,70,13;7bgn,68,12;6ocv,55,6;rtq,55,3;7j4j,55,2;80h1,54,6;5jhi,53,2;3mdj,52,4~6tvj,39,373;a106,21,189;i5v,47,109;aiv4,48,99;1xgr,33,92;ix3,48,83;9elm,15,58;40qz,70,56;93zz,25,47;6qkj,14,45;1eih,91,41;93jo,42,35;5a7n,9,33;11hf,13,30;1qgk,0,19	N:2cbn,137,14;2qb4,119,99;67wv,117,12;4plb,105,4;5655,95,7;1kqf,91,6;90sl,91,6;68s7,90,30;5a7n,88,7544;ne3,86,8;5ldi,80