ix3|v|To take by the arm; to take up in one's arms. ; To furnish with arms or limbs. ; To furnish or equip with weapons of offense or defense; as, to arm soldiers; to arm the country. ; To cover or furnish with a plate, or with whatever will add strength, force, security, or efficiency; as, to arm the hit of a sword; to arm a hook in angling. ; Fig.: To furnish with means of defense; to prepare for resistance; to fortify, in a moral sense. ; To provide one's self with arms, weapons, or means of attack or resistance; to take arms.	o:4s47,74,2;9vnm,62,3;amx3,54,7;4673,51,1;agc2,48,1;167s,45,3;amx5,41,1;2ma,38,2;2q4h,38,1;amx8,35,6;as0e,26,4;4bj4,24,6;68vf,20,4;75pk,18,1;9bci,16,2~7fie,13,10;112e,11,10;amx3,54,7;4bj4,24,6;amx8,35,6;68vf,20,4;112z,0,4;i15,4,4;rg5,2,4;as0e,26,4;62fn,3,3;9vnm,62,3;167s,45,3;8te5,11,2;4s47,74,2	s:3u7k,100,6;75p1,73,4;83oh,56,10;5jls,43,4;51k2,43,1;5p87,35,3;6q8j,27,3;9u2y,27,1;57iy,25,12;1hip,24,2;75me,24,10;5jhi,23,1;83lj,23,5;6os2,22,9;1841,15,2~9qh2,7,90;57iy,25,12;83oh,56,10;75me,24,10;6os2,22,9;3u7k,100,6;9tm9,1,6;83lj,23,5;5jls,43,4;1xpq,9,4;75p1,73,4;5p87,35,3;6q8j,27,3;4bj4,14,3;1hip,24,2	d:a1o1,71,1;3q3o,50,4;57iy,41,36~57iy,41,36;3q3o,50,4;a1o1,71,1	D:3s74,83,1~3s74,83,1
